         [38;5;246mA runner, test layout, and a first passing test. The rules module is pure logic — this is where the real bugs [39m
         [38;5;246mwould be.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Lint + auto-format (Recommended)
         [38;5;246mESLint + Prettier with a strict config. Cheapest to adopt before any code exists.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
         [38;5;246mPlaywright driving a real browser. Catches storage and rendering integration, but heavier for a static page [39m
         [38;5;246mthis size.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — keep it bare
         [38;5;246mNo toolchain at all. Fastest to start, but the rules logic ships unverified and the tax compounds.[39m
